<title>ITALY: IFIL says to have 20 pct of Worms-St Louis.</title>
<headline>IFIL says to have 20 pct of Worms-St Louis.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian financial holding company IFIL said it will have a 20 percent stake in the new company resulting from the merger of French groups Worms and Saint Louis.</p>
<p>IFIL added in a statement that it &quot;will not act in concert&quot; with the Worms family group in the merger company.  </p>
<p>Earlier on Friday, Worms &amp; Cie and Saint Louis said they planned a full merger in which Saint Louis would be absorbed into Worms. The merger had been approved by both boards.</p>
<p>Prior to the merger, IFIL held 7.8 percent of Worms &amp; Cie and 26.5 percent of St Louis. The Worms family will hold some 22 percent in the new merged company.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
